    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0070" n="66" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg66"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.116/156: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic and
                        Consular Officers in China and Japan</hi><anchor n="98" xml:id="d87-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-13T16:00:00-05:00">October 13, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Peiping’s 606, October 6, 6 p.m., Tokyo’s 640 [<hi rendition="#italic">646</hi>],
                    October 6, 9 a.m., and Tientsin’s 191, October 7, 5 p.m., and 192, October 8,
                        noon,<anchor n="99" xml:id="d87-f2"/> in regard to importation of radio
                    equipment. The Department requests that Tokyo notify the Japanese Foreign Office
                    that the proposed arrangements are not satisfactory and that the American
                    Government reserves all rights in respect of losses suffered by American
                    interests in consequence of enforcement by the provisional régime of any
                    restrictions on the importation of American radio equipment.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d87-f3"/></p>
                <p>Peiping repeat to Tientsin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d87-f1" n="98" type="source" xml:id="d87-f1-content">
                <p>At Peiping, Chungking, Tokyo, and Shanghai.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d87-f2" n="99" xml:id="d87-f2-content">
                <p>Last three telegrams not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d87-f3" n="1" xml:id="d87-f3-content">
                <p>The Ambassador in Japan addressed a note to the Japanese Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs on October 18.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
